@b8zhong this implements the two independent model-level precision fixes you called out in #38695: keeping correction bias fp32 in MiMo-V2/Ernie4/Kimi Linear, and removing the fp32-router-logit downcast in Bailing/Bailing Linear/LLaDA2.

@Fridge003 @ishandhanani @Qiaolin-Yu could one of the NV/model-specific optimization oncalls review the scope and contract? The patch is limited to the six model gates plus one registered CPU regression test. All changed files pass the full local pre-commit hook set, bytecode compilation, and `git diff --check`.

The current red matrix entries are PR-gate authorization failures and the registered CPU test was skipped. If the direction looks right, could a maintainer authorize `base-a-test-cpu` / add the `run-ci` label? Thanks.

